  (a) helium: R1-lit Y_P = 0.0000 vs 0.245 +- 0.003: pull +81.7 sigma   (standard BBN, XR26: 0.2467, -0.57 sigma)
  (b) deuterium: R1-lit D/H = 0.000e+00 vs 2.547e-05 +- 2.9e-07: pull +87.8 sigma   (standard BBN, XR26 PArthENoPE: 2.5875e-05, -1.39 sigma)
  (e) neutrino background: R1-lit N_eff = 0.0 vs 2.99 +- 0.17: pull +17.6 sigma (neutrinos decouple at T ~ 1 MeV, z ~ 6e9)
      helium-by-stars energetics (reported; the concept is memory, UNVERIFIED): fusing 0.245 of all baryons releases 6.590e-14 J/m^3 today-equivalent = 1.58 x the CMB energy density (4.175e-14); released at z_f it is diluted by (1 + z_f).  Stellar helium arrives with metals (dY/dZ ~ 1-3, memory UNVERIFIED) while Y_P is measured at very low metallicity.
  (f) blackbody (reported, not a pull): FIRAS |mu| < 9e-5, |y| < 1.5e-5 (memory, UNVERIFIED).  A blackbody made in equilibrium at z* is compatible with R1-om; the acoustic phases and the super-horizon TE correlation (memory, UNVERIFIED) are what separate R1-lit from R1-om.
  G1 classes (R1-lit): (a) Y_P +81.7 sigma CONTRADICTS; (b) D/H +87.8 sigma CONTRADICTS; (c) theta_* +3470.3 sigma CONTRADICTS; (d) BAO r_d +167.2 sigma CONTRADICTS; (e) N_eff +17.6 sigma CONTRADICTS
  R1-lit: FAILS G1 -> CONTRADICTED
  R1-om ('created as if' with a past): matches every observation the standard past matches, by construction -> UNTESTABLE-AS-STATED; a restatement of the standard past.

